    "pathway_role_summary": "WNT3 is a canonical Wnt ligand that initiates the Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway essential for embryonic development, axis specification, and stem cell maintenance. Upon secretion, WNT3 binds to Frizzled receptors and LRP5/6 coreceptors, triggering recruitment of Dishevelled, inhibition of the beta-catenin destruction complex, and subsequent beta-catenin nuclear translocation to activate TCF/LEF-dependent transcription. WNT3 signaling is critical for gastrulation, mesoderm formation, limb development, and maintenance of stem cell populations in adult tissues."
  },
