    "data_quality_notes": "High-quality structural data available (PDB 6AHY). Extensive quantitative binding affinity data for FZD interactions (Kd values 1.5-30 nM range). Post-translational modification sites (C77, S209) well-characterized experimentally. Limited information on other PTM sites beyond lipidation. No high-throughput protein-protein interaction data from BioGRID/IntAct available, relying primarily on STRING and literature. Isoform information not available in UniProt.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "WNT3 is a prototypical canonical Wnt ligand essential for modeling Wnt/beta-catenin signaling dynamics. Key features for modeling: (1) Quantitative FZD binding affinities enabling parameter estimation for receptor-ligand interactions; (2) Essential lipid modifications (C77, S209) providing regulatory control points; (3) Complex trafficking pathway (PORCN->WLS->secretion) enabling secretion regulation modeling; (4) Negative feedback through RNF43/ZNRF3 and positive potentiation via RSPO/LGR providing regulatory loops; (5) Well-defined downstream signaling through DVL, beta-catenin stabilization, and TCF/LEF transcription. Crystal structure with FZD8 provides molecular-level insights into receptor engagement mechanism."
  }
